Chapter: WhenArmNonTail
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A codegen regression. A recursive function whose body is a `when`
 needs its return address saved when an arm makes a NON-tail call, even
 though another arm makes a tail call that would let it skip the frame's
 ra. my-filter is the smallest shape: the ICons arm's then-branch conses
 the recursive result (`ICons h (my-filter pred t)`, non-tail) while its
 else-branch is a tail call. On RISC-V the plug's ra-need analysis had no
 IrMatch arm, answered "no ra needed", elided the save, and my-filter
 looped back into itself on return -- stopping the program mid-output.
 my-map (arm conses a value, no tail call) always worked; sum-real (a
 pure tail loop, no non-tail call) must keep skipping ra. Reduced from
 list-test.

Section: Loop

  IntList =
   | INil
   | ICons (Integer) (IntList)

  is-even : Integer -> Boolean
  is-even (n) = (n / 2) * 2 == n

  dbl : Integer -> Integer
  dbl (n) = n * 2

  my-sum : IntList -> Integer
  my-sum (xs) =
   when xs
    is ICons (h) (t) -> h + my-sum t
    is INil -> 0

  my-map : (Integer -> Integer), IntList -> IntList
  my-map (f) (xs) =
   when xs
    is ICons (h) (t) -> ICons (f h) (my-map f t)
    is INil -> INil

  my-filter : (Integer -> Boolean), IntList -> IntList
  my-filter (pred) (xs) =
   when xs
    is ICons (h) (t) -> if pred h then ICons h (my-filter pred t) else my-filter pred t
    is INil -> INil

  sum-real : IntList, Integer -> Integer
  sum-real (xs) (acc) =
   when xs
    is ICons (h) (t) -> sum-real t (acc + h)
    is INil -> acc

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let nums = ICons 1 (ICons 2 (ICons 3 (ICons 4 (ICons 5 INil))))
    in act
     print-line-uni ("map-sum: " & show (my-sum (my-map dbl nums)))
     print-line-uni ("filter-sum: " & show (my-sum (my-filter is-even nums)))
     print-line-uni ("tail-loop: " & show (sum-real nums 100))
    end
  end
